      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Chapterhouse of the Fallen [zone=874]\n**Who:**\n- Sir Birton [npc=41326]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Burning Dead Robes [item=106473]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Falsin Bonecraft [npc=42313]\n- Orson Gravegloom [npc=41332]\n- Plinki Bonebrood [npc=41331]\n- Yarin Shroudfear [npc=41330]\n**Related Quests:**\n- A Matter of Life and Death [quest=6104]\n- Breaking Bones [quest=6099]\n- Chapterhouse #2: Operation [quest=6101]\n- Chapterhouse #3: Dead Gnomes Tell No Tales... Or Do They? [quest=6102]\n- Organ Trail [quest=6100]\n- Raid Expedition: A Matter of Life and Death [quest=6105]\n- Run, You Fools! [quest=6103]\n- Undead Maintenance [quest=6098]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 05:46:57 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task begins with Sir Birton ( map) in the Chapterhouse of the Fallen. He is found at location 65, 545, 0 (on the main floor are two large rooms -- he is in the northwest part of the west room)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- No tasks\nYou say, 'Hail, Sir Birton'\nSir Birton says 'Stay your weapons; I have no intent on harming you. A much greater [threat] dwells in the depths of these once sacred halls.'\nYou say, 'What threat?'\nSir Birton says 'The necromancers of the Burning Dead have infiltrated the lower levels, and seek to raise the dead for some nefarious scheme. We must find a way to stop them. No; you must find a way to [stop them].'\nYou say, 'How do we stop them?'\nSir Birton says 'If you are not afraid of the walking dead, and if you are, I don't know why you have traveled here, you must find a way to infiltrate the ranks of the Burning Dead and discover their plans. I may have a way to help you gain access to one of their leaders, [Falsin Bonecraft].'\nYou say, 'Who is Falsin Bonecraft?'\nSir Birton says 'Falsin is a despicable little gnome who delights in having undead servants do his dirty work. However, I do not think he would be opposed to having a new gnomish recruit if the opportunity presented itself. Will you help to [infiltrate] the ranks of the Burning Dead?'\nYou say, 'I will infiltrate them'\nSir Birton says 'I knew I could count on you. Take these Burning Dead robes. When used, they will cast an illusion spell upon you so that you can blend in among the necromancers. The undead however may see through your disguise, so use caution. If you [need more robes] just let me know and I will give you some more. That is all. May Marr's blessing be upon you.'\n_You receive \"Burning Dead Robes\"._\nYou have been assigned the task 'Infiltrating the Burning Dead'.\nAn undead paladin named Sir Birton has asked you to infiltrate the Burning Dead cult that has spread throughout the deeper regions of the Chapterhouse.\nUse the Burning Dead Robes to disguise yourself as a member of the Burning Dead and speak with Falsin Bonecraft.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with the leader of the Burning Dead, Falsin Bonecraft 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_Falsin Bonecraft ( map) is found at /location 0, 815, -91 (down one level from the main floor -- the western half of that level)._\n_Use the illusion before speaking to him._\nYou say, 'Hail, Falsin Bonecraft'\nFalsin Bonecraft says 'Ah, another initiate eager to prove their worth to the Burning Dead? So be it. There is a lot to be done before the ritual commences, and you will prove your worth by completing some tasks given by some of my neophytes. Seek out Yarin Shroudfear, Plinki Bonebrood, and Orson Gravegloom and do what they say. Disobey, and I will kill you and then reanimate your bones to clean the latrines. Now go.'\nSpeak with Yarin Shroudfear 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nYou say, 'Hail, Yarin Shroudfear'\nYarin Shroudfear says 'Falsin sent you to help me? Good, I am very busy and there are lots of things that need to be done. Some of the mummies need their linen wrappings changed, the ghouls need to be fed, and some of the zombies need some pep, as they are becoming too complacent. Give them some of this energy elixir. Let me know if you need more [linen wrappings], [rotten flesh], or [energy elixir]. Oh, I almost forgot; there is also a skeleton that has become too intelligent and continues to resist our efforts to control him. Seek out Coffinhowl and destroy him.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Undead Maintenance'.\nComplete the task that Yarin Shroudfear has assigned to you 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_Complete the task \" Undead Maintenance [quest=6098]\"._\nSpeak with Plinki Bonebrood 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nYou say, 'Hail, Plinki Bonebrood'\nPlinki Bonebrood says 'Some of our more unconventional experiments have gone awry. Seek out these failed experiments and destroy them. And make sure to kill the neophyte responsible for these failed experiments. His name is Jurso Fumblefink.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Breaking Bones'.\nComplete the task that Plinki Bonebrood has assigned to you 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_Complete the task \" Breaking Bones [quest=6099]\"._\nSpeak with Orson Gravegloom 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nYou say, 'Hail, Orson Gravegloom'\nOrson Gravegloom says 'Oh, hello. I'm Orson. The others here like to make fun of me because they think I am not so smart, but I will prove them wrong! In the meantime, can you [take care] of something for me? I am way behind in my studies and if I raise another zombie that decides it would rather recite poetry than act all zombie-like, I will fail my exam again.'\nYou say, 'I'd love to take care of it...'\nOrson Gravegloom says 'We need lots of organs for some sort of upcoming ritual. I'm not sure what it's all about, but I am sure it will be all gory and stuff. We will need an appendix, a spleen, a liver, a tongue, a pair of eyes, a spinal cord, and a heart. I was told that the heart we need belongs to a paladin named, Sir Graxton Talonheart. He probably wants to keep his heart, so expect a fight. Once you have all that stuff, place everything into the coffin nearby. Why? I don't know, just cause that's what you're supposed to do.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Organ Trail'.\nComplete the task that Orson Gravegloom has assigned to you 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_Complete the task \" Organ Trail [quest=6100]\"._\nSpeak with Sir Birton 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nYou say, 'Hail, Sir Birton'\nSir Birton says 'My sources inform me that you have blended in well with the Burning Dead and are well on your way to getting on their good side; if they have one that is. I just hope you didn't enjoy your grisly tasks too much. There is still much to be done before you fully gain their trust however. We must find out more about their upcoming ritual. Use the burning dead robes to disguise yourself again and seek out a necromancer known as Bertrand the Butcher. I hear he is eager to show new recruits the tricks of the trade. Gain his trust and hopefully we can learn more about the upcoming ritual. If you [need more robes] just let me know.'\n_Rewards:_\n450 platinum\nExperience (6 AAs)",
