spinal cord, and a heart. I was told that the heart we need belongs to a paladin named, Sir Graxton Talonheart. He probably wants to keep his heart, so expect a fight. Once you have all that stuff, place everything into the coffin nearby. Why? I don't know, just cause that's what you're supposed to do.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Organ Trail'.\nOrson Gravegloom has asked you to complete a task that he doesn't have time to do himself.\nFind an appendix, a spleen, a liver, a tongue, a pair of eyes, and a spinal cord, and then place them in the coffin near Orson Gravegloom. These parts are scattered throughout the tunnels that the Burning Dead inhabit as well as the prison area. Locate the imprisoned paladin, Sir Graxton Talondrake, and then take his heart.\n\n---\n\nPlace an appendix inside the coffin 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nPlace a spleen inside the coffin 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nPlace a liver inside the coffin 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nPlace a tongue inside the coffin 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nPlace a pair of eyes inside the coffin 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nPlace a spinal cord inside the coffin 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_The above six items are scattered throughout the area as ground spawns (appear as hunks of meat on the ground)._\nKill Sir Graxton Talondrake and take his heart 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_Sir Graxton Talondrake ( map) is found in a prison cell on the same floor, but on the eastern side (you will have to leave the floor and reach the prison through either the basement caverns or the main floor)._\n_He is found at /location 225, 60, -91 (the first cell to the east from the north entrance to the prison area). Note that while he is KOS, he is not social with any other mobs in the zone._\nPlace Sir Graxton's heart inside the coffin 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_Rewards:_\n\\- Progresses the task \"Infiltrating the Burning Dead\"",
