      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Chapterhouse of the Fallen [zone=874]\n**Who:**\n- Holy Defender Ioris [npc=41329]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Chapterhouse: Run, You Fools! [zone=895]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- High Lord William Taros [npc=42677]\n- Holy Defender Ioris [npc=42686]\n- Menizzia [npc=42672]\n- a bloodthirsty ghoul - Chapterhouse of the Fallen [npc=42685]\n- a corrupt paladin [npc=42682]\n- a corrupted poltergeist [npc=42684]\n- a deathly shadow [npc=42688]\n- a fallen defender [npc=42675]\n- a fleshrend beetle [npc=42674]\n- a lost spirit of light [npc=42681]\n- a shambling corpse [npc=42676]\n- a summoned skeleton [npc=42687]\n- a vile priest [npc=42680]\n- a wrapped soul [npc=42683]\n- an animated corpse [npc=42689]\n- an old chest - Run, You Fools! [npc=42466]\n- an undead lord [npc=42678]\n- an undead noble [npc=42679]\n- corpse of Marnek [npc=42673]\n**Related Quests:**\n- A Matter of Life and Death [quest=6104]\n- Chapterhouse #1: Infiltrating the Burning Dead [quest=6097]\n- Chapterhouse #2: Operation [quest=6101]\n- Chapterhouse #3: Dead Gnomes Tell No Tales... Or Do They? [quest=6102]\n- Raid Expedition: A Matter of Life and Death [quest=6105]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 29 05:47:25 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This group mission begins with Holy Defender Ioris ( map) in the Chapterhouse of the Fallen at location -125, -70, -1 -- in the side room just north of the zone-in from the Commonlands (southeast of the Shard's Landing portal)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"Infiltrating the Burning Dead\"\n\\- Completed \"Operation\"\n\\- Completed \"Dead Gnomes Tell No Tales... Or Do They?\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Holy Defender Ioris'\nHoly Defender Ioris nods in acknowledgement of your greeting. 'You're really earning a name for yourself, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Sir Birton has informed me that your infiltration efforts are the reason we were able to uncover Menizzia's [plot].\nYou say, 'What plot?'\nHoly Defender Ioris says 'Menizzia plans to raise an ancient necromancer by the name of Marnek Jaull. His summoning must be stopped. It is not a task I can accomplish alone, however.'\nBloodreaver Narek smiles slyly, 'If you need the assistance of a Knight of Innoruuk, all you need to do is ask, Ioris.'\nHoly Defender Ioris focuses her stern gaze straight ahead, refusing to look Narek in the eye. 'A Paladin of Marr does not require help from those that commune with the dead.'\nBloodreaver Narek says 'As you wish. But heed this warning Ioris; if the summoning succeeds, Marnek Jaull will have power within the realm of the living, as well as the dead. You may find someone with my...' A smooth smile spreads across the shadowknight's face, '...skills, handy.''\nHoly Defender Ioris shivers at the thought before turning her attention toward you, 'Enough of the idle chatter. I will take care of Mezinnia myself if I have to, but I'm counting on your [help], \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nYou say, 'I will help'\nHoly Defender Ioris nods. 'We should make haste then. Mezzinia has likely already begun her ritual. Let me know when you are ready to [enter] the summoning chamber.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Run, You Fools!'.\nFind Menizzia and put a stop to her attempt to summon Marnek Jaull. Destroy Menizzia's minions and then press the attack upon her.\nYou say, 'Let' enter!'\nHoly Defender Ioris says 'This way then. I hope you can swim, as much of the path is under water.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Chapterhouse of the Fallen.\n\n---\n\nFind Menizzia 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_From the zone-in, head up the ramp and into Menizzia's room. Three aggro mobs spawn and attack._\nMenizzia shouts 'NO! The resurrection must not be interrupted. Marnek MUST rise again! Perhaps this will keep you occupied while I complete the ritual!'\n\n---\n\nDestroy Menizzia's minions 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_Kill the three mobs (simple fights). Upon the death of the last mob, be ready to move and keep moving until you reach the end of the task. (If you stop or slow down at any point, it will result in your group's deaths._\na fleshrend beetle has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na fleshrend beetle's corpse shudders and falls to the ground\na fallen defender has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na fallen defender's corpse collapses to the ground\na shambling corpse has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na shambling corpse's corpse stumbles and falls\nMenizzia shouts 'Ridiculous! Will these interruptions never end? Perhaps I need to turn up the heat a bit. Lord Taros will make short work of you!'\nHoly Defender Ioris' voice seems to float through your mind, \"Do not engage Lord Taros, as he is not one to be trifled with. You MUST flee if you can.\"\nHigh Lord William Taros shouts 'Flee while you can, insects! You only delay the inevitable.'\n\n---\n\nEscape from Lord Taros 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_Task Window Says:_ Menizzia has summoned High Lord William Taros, a fallen knight of incredible power. You cannot possibly hope to defeat him now. Run, for your lives!\n_You'll need to avoid Taros without getting too close to him (damage aura) or too far behind him (death touch) while clearing the area of mobs._\n_From Menizzia's room: Head through the east tunnel, fight the single mob there, and then go into the second room. Kill five mobs there._\n_From the second room: Head through the north tunnel and into the third room. Kill four mobs there._\n_From the third room: Head into the tunnel to your west, to the end of it, fight the single mob there, and then into the connecting room to that tunnel's south. This is the final room (a few more mobs to kill)._\n_Once in this room, wait for Lord Taros to catch up, and for the script to unfold. Afterwards, Menizzia goes aggro._\n_Note: For reference points, see the map associated with Braintaster. His northeastern spawn location is the \"third room\" as described above. His southwestern spawn location is the final room._\n_As you make your way through the task, you'll see emotes (just flavor text):_\nHigh Lord William Taros shouts 'Run away, little meat sacks!'\nHigh Lord William Taros shouts 'Do you not feel the hand of death closing around your neck? Soon you will be nothing but worm food!'\nHigh Lord William Taros shouts 'Try to flee if you must. Death marches on. None can escape my blade!'\n_Upon reaching the final room and killing the mobs there:_\nHigh Lord William Taros shouts 'I see our little chase has come to the inevitable end. There will be no escape this time. Take your last, pointless breaths while you still can!'\nHoly Defender Ioris shouts 'Not so fast Taros! These brave adventurers will NOT fall today. Not if I have anything to say about it!'\nHigh Lord William Taros shouts 'The living are so predictable. I will not be deterred, not by the likes of you, Ioris!'\nHoly Defender Ioris shouts 'Death has addled what brain you once had, Taros. Come, feel the might of my blade!'\nHoly Defender Ioris shouts 'You there, I will keep Taros occupied. You must return to Menizzia and stop the resurrection of Marnek at any cost, even your own lives! All will perish if Marnek returns!'\nMenizzia shouts 'Did someone call my name? Your efforts here have all been for naught. Marnek lives again, and nothing you do here can change that, yet clearly I cannot trust this walking bag of bones to dispatch the likes of you. Better I deal with you myself and be done with it!'\nMenizzia shouts 'I may not be able to destroy you Ioris, but this is MY realm, and you have no power here. Begone!'\nMenizzia banishes Holy Defender Ioris and saps any remaining energy from Taros in the process. Taros falls to the ground in a heap of lifeless bones.\nHigh Lord William Taros collapses to the ground\nHigh Lord William Taros died.\nMenizzia shouts 'Now then, I will deal with you fleshlings. Marnek lives, you will die, and nothing will stand in my way any longer!'\n_Menizzia goes auto-aggro and attacks._\n\n---\n\nKill Menizzia once and for all 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\n_Menizzia hits for a max ~18,000. She also has a run-away emote (flashes on screen), a 9-second warning preceding a 50' range AE nuke for 150,000hp:_\nMenizzia begins to pulse with the fury of the dead. You should probably run away!\nNecromantic Fury: PB AE 50', (0)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 150000\nNecromantic energy explodes outward from Menizzia melting all living flesh in range.\n_Every 45 seconds, she spawns 1x \"a deathly shadow\" + 1x \"an animated corpse\". These need to be killed. If left alive, they despawn with an AE + heal on Menizzia:_\nCorpse Explosion: PB AE 100', (0)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 50000\n_As Menizzia's health lowers, she will occasionally spawn a wave of 5x \"a summoned skeleton\":_\nMenizzia shouts 'Why must I waste my time with you? Perhaps some more of my minions will help relieve you of your mortal coil?!'\n_Kill her to update this step:_\nMenizzia has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nMenizzia's corpse collapses to the ground.\n\n---\n\nOpen the old chest and claim your reward 0/1 (Chapterhouse of the Fallen)\nYou have defeated Menizzia, but unfortunately she was able to summon Marnek Jaull before you dispatched her.\n_Rewards:_\n150 platinum\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Dreadmote per task):_\nFang Whistle\nForce of Two\nGentleman's Flair\nMedal of Honor\nOssein Cloak\nPain Nullifier\nXanture's Lens of Untold Secrets\nLesser Dreadmote\nMedian Dreadmote\nGreater Dreadmote\nGlowing Dreadmote\n- Force of Two [item=108203]\n- Glowing Dreadmote [item=106497]\n- Greater Dreadmote [item=106464]\n- Lesser Dreadmote [item=106476]\n- Medal of Honor [item=108122]\n- Median Dreadmote [item=106509]\n- Ossein Cloak [item=109239]\n- Pain Nullifier [item=108410]\n- Xanture's Lens of Untold Secrets [item=110330]",
